Subject: Cantor SJS Commit Placement Acquisition P3 Input Audit

@ [audit_uuid] 3f73360b-b13d-4cfc-9aa7-1612f60b0e74
@ [canonical_uuid] 7602b617-05c5-459a-8a78-23bcd638e164

& [Authority]
  + active Pinky source authority and Cantor overlay are applied
  + source preservation precedes SJS and satisfaction protocol ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c is required
  + P0 P1 and P2 published semantics are predecessor constraints rather than editable inputs

& [InputClassification]
  + dictated objective is physical read-only verification of supplied P2 placement before SWA-05
  + physical Git observation is in scope only after signature
  + repository mutation broker authorization provider activation and self-signature are out of scope

& [Gap]
  + P2 proves supplied-data chain consistency but cannot prove that a carrier commit parent tree path or blob physically exists
  + P1 observes only the current staged index and cannot prove published commit-tree placement
  + the smallest missing seam is an exact carrier commit tree blob observer rather than a publisher

& [SelectedInterpretation]
  + embed and verify the complete P2 journal before process contact
  + require expected HEAD equals the P2 open carrier tip
  + encode each record as compact serde JSON plus one LF and compare exact blob bytes
  + return observation-only evidence without transforming the P2 supplied placement into broker authority

& [RejectedAlternatives]
  + same-commit closure because P2 already proves the digest recursion
  + Git notes sidecar config or custom object writes because they mutate repository state
  + shell PATH Git ambient config textconv filters and worktree reads because they weaken executable and blob identity
  + accepting blob hash without exact bytes because canonical serialization drift could be hidden
  + importing human SOP bookends as machine P2 records because their byte form is different
